// The DIP example (Section 3 of the paper), the repaired version: a Vehicle interface owned by the manager, which the vehicles implement.
// Two axes: the vehicles change more often (new kinds) and are easier to change than the manager.
axis transport = [martin.dip.transport]
axis vehicles  = [martin.dip.vehicles]
// the speed order; it generates hide vehicles from transport
speed transport < vehicles;
